{"title":"Cartesian product","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Cartesian product</b> of two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">sets</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the set of all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ordered_pair\" title=\"Ordered pair\">ordered pairs</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Element\" title=\"Element\">element</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Element\" title=\"Element\">element</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.  More generally, the Cartesian product of an ordered family of sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1977acebd8b25dc1d3f3e5632718f0deba6e5e60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, \\dotsc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> is the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda77c5555587f9713a54697cab04c1581cf4486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 \\times A_2 \\times \\dotsb$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" /> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ordered_tuples\" title=\"Ordered tuples\">ordered tuples</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b81c7244893004e622071559e0c43f147df9f106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1, a_2, \\dotsb)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> is an element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edb286660f22d694ff4152ede3c948864cbb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />, for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> for which we have specified a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edb286660f22d694ff4152ede3c948864cbb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Existence\">Existence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_product&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Existence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_product&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binary_relation\" title=\"Binary relation\">Binary relation</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_product&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211632\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 87/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2464/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.324      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.324      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5829:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017211632 and revision id 225984. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}